; A two-member map in which each member declares a located hole
; (lara-core@0.3, spec §4.4). Both members are accepted on their own and the
; linked unit is accepted with two holes. The committed map.verdict.sexp pins
; map-verdict@2's two hole decisions: nodes/labels/edges share the AF index
; space (paper_pos's complete `pa` is AF node 0 although `ph` precedes it), and
; every hole is reported by (member alias, member-local argument id) with its
; exact obligations. map.core.sexp is the parity envelope the Lean driver reads.
(lara-map@1
  (policy empirical-v1 empirical-v1.policy.lara)
  (backends (backend nd 1))
  (members
    (member paper_pos pos.lara)
    (member paper_neg neg.lara))
  (alignments
    (alignment
      (ref paper_pos c_pos whole)
      (ref paper_neg c_neg whole)
      different
      (author reviewer_r)
      (audit-status reviewed)
      (rationale "The two papers state opposite results about the same system, measurand and dataset.")))
  (questions))
